WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.230
The Site Allocations Plan is a list of
predominantly housing sites that would

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.250
come forward if we were unable to
deliver a five-year housing land supply

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.150
as required by the Core Strategy. We're
not in that position; we have a really

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.320
strong five-year housing land supply and
that's evidenced by the fact that within

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.060
the last three months a developer
brought forward an appeal based on

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.060
challenging our five-year housing land
supply. When they saw our numbers they

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.340
abandoned the appeal, so that's a really
strong place to start with. Secondly, we

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.660
have a set of allocated sites already in
the Core Strategy which are on track

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.890
for delivery and as long as those sites
are delivered there is no need for us to

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.660
consider any of the reserve sites. The
third area where sites could come

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.800
forward would be under what's called a
duty to cooperate. In short, if Birmingham

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.370
and Coventry can't demonstrate they've
got sufficient land to meet their needs,

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:55.350
as a neighbouring authority we have to
help out. The good news is we'd already

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:59.340
factored in a number of houses and have
delivered a number of houses to meet

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.420
that anticipated need, so we're a really
long way from ever having to be in that

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.530
position and if anybody tried to bring a
site forward they would have to

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:12.150
demonstrate that firstly Birmingham or
Coventry had asked for and requested us

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.920
to cooperate, and that there was no other
mechanism to deliver those houses within

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.420
the Core Strategy as it currently stands,
so the bar is set really high in terms

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:27.180
of bringing any of those sites on stream. The Site Allocations Plan identifies a 20%

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:32.100
buffer which is circa 3,000 homes. As I
said earlier on this is a reserve list,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.229
the bar is set extremely high, and
there's a mechanism to ensure that when

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:42.000
people try to bring these sites forward
they have to hit certain checkmarks

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.470
around the five year land supply, duty to
cooperate, and we are nowhere near that,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:51.899
so I am absolutely confident. There are
nearly 500 homes in my own ward

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:57.360
in Bidford identified in this plan and
I'm completely satisfied that the sites

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.040
are very unlikely ever to come forward
within this Core Strategy period. I'd

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:08.250
like to send a message out to land
owners, to property developers, and also

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:12.900
to our local communities: this reserve
list is exactly what it says - it's a

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.030
reserve list.
There is no need for us to bring these

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:21.160
sites forward as long as we deliver the
sites that are already allocated. So, if

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.930
you're a landowner, if you're a developer,
don't waste your time, don't waste your

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:29.560
money, and don't waste the effort of this
council's officers in bringing sites

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.090
forward which have no prospect
whatsoever of coming forward as

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.690
development sites within the Core
Strategy period up to 2031.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.920
I would also add that we are obliged to
undertake a review of the Core Strategy,

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:48.070
which will happen in 2020. That Core
Strategy review will undoubtedly look to

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:52.900
change the shape of future development
and will ultimately lead post-2031 to a

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:58.090
new Core Strategy so although we have to
go through this exercise, this set of

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:03.870
sites could well be redundant early into
next year.

